To get that exact same "19 Jun 2026, 12:58 pm" format with the capitalized month, we just need to swap out the native toLocaleString function and use the formatDateTime function we just updated!
I highly recommend updating it in **two** places so that your entire screen (the grid and the modal) matches perfectly.
### 1. Update the Voucher Request ID "Created At" in the Modal
Find the Grid item for the Voucher "Created At" (around line 1025) and replace it.
**FIND THIS:**
```javascript
                        <Grid item xs={12} sm={3}>
                          <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block" gutterBottom>
                            Created At
                          </Typography>
                          <Typography variant="body1" fontWeight="500">
                            {vidDetails.VID_CREATED_AT
                              ? new Date(vidDetails.VID_CREATED_AT).toLocaleString("en-IN", {
                                dateStyle: "short",
                                timeStyle: "short",
                              })
                              : "N/A"}
                          </Typography>
                        </Grid>

```
**REPLACE WITH THIS:**
```javascript
                        <Grid item xs={12} sm={3}>
                          <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block" gutterBottom>
                            Created At
                          </Typography>
                          <Typography variant="body1" fontWeight="500">
                            {vidDetails.VID_CREATED_AT
                              ? formatDateTime(vidDetails.VID_CREATED_AT)
                              : "N/A"}
                          </Typography>
                        </Grid>

```
